{"name":"Woodland Walk","hex":"#8b8d63","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woodland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a creature or object: growing, living, or existing in a woodland.","Having the character of a woodland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Land covered with woody vegetation.","A low-density forest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woodland"},{"term":"walk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move on the feet by alternately setting each foot (or pair or group of feet: in the case of some non-human animals with four or more feet) forward, with at least one foot on the ground at all times. Compare run.","To \"walk free\", i.e. to win, or avoid, a criminal court case, particularly when actually guilty."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trip made by walking.","A distance walked."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Downham Woodland Walk","blocks":[{"text":"Downham Woodland Walk is a linear park and local nature reserve in Downham in the London Borough of Lewisham. It is also a Site of Borough Importance for Nature Conservation, Grade 1. The site is owned and managed by Lewisham Council."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Downham_Woodland_Walk_3.JPG/330px-Downham_Woodland_Walk_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Downham_Woodland_Walk","wikidata":"Q16989038"},{"title":"Woodland","blocks":[{"text":"A woodland is, in the broad sense, land covered with woody plants, or in a narrow sense, synonymous with wood, a low-density forest forming open habitats with plenty of sunlight and limited shade. Some savannas may also be woodlands, such as savanna woodland, where trees and shrubs form a light canopy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg/330px-Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodland","wikidata":"Q3241565"},{"title":"Walking","blocks":[{"text":"Walking is one of the main gaits of terrestrial locomotion among legged animals. Walking is typically slower than running and other gaits. Walking is defined as an \"inverted pendulum\" gait in which the body vaults over the stiff limb or limbs with each step. This applies regardless of the usable number of limbs—even arthropods, with six, eight, or more limbs, walk. In humans, limited research indicates that walking may be associated with reduced risk of diseases and premature death."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Women_walking_in_Hyderabad_street.jpg/330px-Women_walking_in_Hyderabad_street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walking","wikidata":"Q6537379"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Nyika_miombo.jpg/500px-Nyika_miombo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Nyika_miombo.jpg/1280px-Nyika_miombo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Nyika_miombo.jpg/500px-Nyika_miombo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Miombo woodland in Malawi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANyika_miombo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg/500px-Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Cumberland_Plains_Woodlands%2C_Prestons_-_2.jpg/1280px-Cumberland